Author: david gauchard <gauchard@laas.fr>
Date: 2022-05-11 16:00:22 +0200
Subject: make `sys_now()` an always inlined function (d-a-v/esp82xx-nonos-linklayer#57)

It was previoulsy a #define as `millis()`
but its return type `u32` is no longer a long but an int, causing third-party troubles.

Only hides real func when definition is not available
This repeats the sys_jiffies block above

Signed-off-by: Maxim Prokhorov <prokhorov.max@outlook.com>

---
 src/include/lwip/sys.h |    2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/include/lwip/sys.h b/src/include/lwip/sys.h
index 168e465ba..0e9e9af8f 100644
--- a/src/include/lwip/sys.h
+++ b/src/include/lwip/sys.h
@@ -443,7 +443,9 @@ u32_t sys_jiffies(void);
  * Not implementing this function means you cannot use some modules (e.g. TCP
  * timestamps, internal timeouts for NO_SYS==1).
  */
+#ifndef sys_now
 u32_t sys_now(void);
+#endif
 
 /* Critical Region Protection */
 /* These functions must be implemented in the sys_arch.c file.
